          "w": 1,
          "h": 1,
          "color": "#153f48",
          "text": "1. Breaking Work Into Parts\nHow does separating the work into parts help with game development?\nMakes big projects easier to manage.\nKeeps everyone organized.\nAllows team members to focus on different tasks.\nHelps identify and fix problems\nMakes it easier to track progress and meet deadlines.\n2. Creativity & Growth Mindset\nBe creative and think outside the box.\nAdapt quickly to changes.\nFocus on your fans and what they enjoy.\nLearn from mistakes and accept feedback.\nTake on challenges and never stop learning.\nSurround yourself with supportive people.\n3. Staying Motivated & Organized\nSet clear goals.\nMake task lists and deadlines.\nStay organized and manage your time.\nPersevere even when things get difficult.\n4. Folder Structure & Sharing\nCreate a main folder with your project name.\nKeep assets, documents, and files organized.\nUse folders to make information easy to find.\nShare organized folders and documents with teammates.\nGood documentation helps new teammembers understand the project.",
          "fill": "#d8e5fb"
        }
